ORIGIN
Caravel is a modified version of Felucca 1.6.1:
  Felucca, Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments
  https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca, tag v1.6.1 (commit a53ecf4), GPL-3.0-only
The work began with Felucca 1.5 in use; the first recorded commit (10 October 2026) builds on Felucca 1.5.1, and the 1.6 and 1.6.1
sources were taken in later. It is released under the name Caravel from version 0.1.0 on. Felucca's active development has ended.
Felucca and Hügelton Instruments are names of Hügelton Instruments. They are used here only to state where this code comes from.

CHANGES (GNU GPL v3, section 5a)
This is not the original Felucca. The initial Caravel changes are recorded as one baseline snapshot on the unchanged public
Felucca 1.6.1 history. That commit identifies the modified files and its preparation date; it does not reconstruct the
individual development dates of those changes. The additions are listed in CHANGELOG.md and described in docs/. Among them: the renaming (display names, version 0.1.0, USB manufacturer / product strings, installer,
editor and emulator texts, package file names), the two-group menu layout, the SEQ CLEAR STEP key, LFO2 and the MOD additions,
the SEM, HADES, DRONE and DRUM-X engines, MORPH, per-track voice reservations and the external-clock fixes.
Files that were changed keep their original copyright and SPDX headers. New files carry "Copyright (C) 2026 bonszaimusic".

DRUM-X AND OTHER JIANT PARTS
DRUM-X (fixed-point synthesis and the factory A/B sounds), MORPH, PHASE feedback and LOFI BYTE/FLOAT are adapted from JIANT FM
(juanjiant-bit/JIANT, GPL-3.0-only, itself a Felucca fork), at the commits named in CREDITS.md. DRUM-X follows the idea of Sonic
Charge's Microtonic (not affiliated); Caravel added track-local kits, fixed MIDI Learn targets and compatible storage.
The BYTE/FLOAT formulas acknowledge Tejeez, xpansive and viznut. Affected source files say so in their headers.

